# Production .env values a service cannot boot without, and that the deploy must
# therefore find BEFORE it builds or recreates anything.
#
# One rule per line:  service|VARIABLE|kind|argument
#
#   hex64     64 hex characters, not all zeros (an AES-256 key). Generated with
#             `openssl rand -hex 32`.
#   password  at least 24 characters and not the committed default `claw_secret`.
#             Generated with `openssl rand -hex 24`.
#   derived   a value built from other variables; the argument is the template and
#             {NAME} is replaced by the value of NAME from the same .env. Used for
#             connection strings, so the URL and the database password cannot
#             drift apart.
#   literal   a fixed, non-secret value; the argument is the exact value. Used for
#             the internal URL a CALLER needs: the shared HTTP client refuses any
#             host not named by a *_SERVICE_URL in the caller's own environment
#             ("refusing a host this service does not call"), so a caller
#             without it cannot reach the service although it is healthy.
#   database  VARIABLE is `-`; the argument is the container name of a database
#             the service needs. The deploy NEVER starts databases (see
#             docs/PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md), so it must already be running and
#             healthy.
#   cert-san  VARIABLE is `-`; the argument is a hostname that certs/claw.crt must
#             list as a DNS subject alternative name. nginx verifies every
#             upstream certificate, so a service missing from the certificate
#             answers 502 although it is healthy. Checked by the deploy only.
#
# Read by scripts/ensure-prod-env.sh (which appends what is missing) and by the
# preflight in scripts/deploy-prod.sh (which refuses to roll out without it).
# Adding a service with a database or a secret means adding its rules here, in
# the same change (docs/11-runbooks/add-a-service-to-production.md).
# Values are never stored in this file and are never printed by either script.

plugin-service|PG_PLUGIN_PASSWORD|password|
plugin-service|PLUGIN_DATABASE_URL|derived|postgresql://claw:{PG_PLUGIN_PASSWORD}@pg-plugin:5432/claw_plugin?schema=public
plugin-service|PLUGIN_ENCRYPTION_KEY|hex64|
plugin-service|-|database|claw-pg-plugin
plugin-service|-|cert-san|plugin-service
health-service|PLUGIN_SERVICE_URL|literal|https://plugin-service:4021
plugin-service|PLUGIN_SERVICE_URL|literal|https://plugin-service:4021
